   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "calloc — a memory allocator",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_53_02\" id=\"tag_17_53_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/stdlib.h.html\">stdlib.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nvoid *calloc(size_t</tt> <i>nelem</i><tt>, size_t</tt> <i>elsize</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_53_03\" id=\"tag_17_53_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]calloc[/I5]() function shall allocate unused space for an array of [I6]nelem[/I6] elements each of whose size in bytes is\n[I7]elsize[/I7]. The space shall be initialized to all bits 0.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The order and contiguity of storage allocated by successive calls to [I8]calloc[/I8]() is unspecified. The pointer returned if the\nallocation succeeds shall be suitably aligned so that it may be assigned to a pointer to any type of object with a fundamental\nalignment requirement and then used to access such an object or an array of such objects in the space allocated (until the space is\nexplicitly freed or reallocated). Each such allocation shall yield a pointer to an object disjoint from any other object. The\npointer returned shall point to the start (lowest byte address) of the allocated space. If the space cannot be allocated, a null\npointer shall be returned. If the size of the space requested is 0, the behavior is implementation-defined: either a null pointer\nshall be returned, or the behavior shall be as if the size were some non-zero value, except that the behavior is undefined if the\nreturned pointer is used to access an object.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "For purposes of determining the existence of a data race, [I9]calloc[/I9]() shall behave as though it accessed only memory\nlocations accessible through its arguments and not other static duration storage. The function may, however, visibly modify the\nstorage that it allocates. Calls to [A10][I11]aligned_alloc[/I11]()[/A10], [I12]calloc[/I12](), [A13][I14]free[/I14]()[/A13], [A15][I16]malloc[/I16]()[/A15], [S17][[A18]ADV[/A18]][/S17] [IMG19] &nbsp;[A20][I21]posix_memalign[/I21]()[/A20], [IMG22]\n\n[S23][[A24]CX[/A24]][/S23] [IMG25]\n[A26][I27]reallocarray[/I27]()[/A26], [IMG28]\n&nbsp;and [A29][I30]realloc[/I30]()[/A29] that allocate or deallocate a particular region of memory shall\noccur in a single total order (see [A31][I32]4.15.1 Memory Ordering[/I32][/A31]), and each\nsuch deallocation call shall synchronize with the next allocation (if any) in this order.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A10": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/aligned_alloc.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
